issues.problem:
Mutation testing (my copy, m2x-v1-3/mutate.py, against `--quick --root tests/Physics`): 910 line mutants of Cover.luau 142-894 and Sampling.luau 481-769; 780 killed, 130 survived. The surviving Cover mutants that change behaviour all sit in the stop at the budget and the report cadence. These survive:
- dropping `return 0, 0, true` (line 503);
- `budget < 0` changed to `<= 0` or `< 1` (502);
- dropping the `return` after `over` at 569, 593, 626, 652, 707, 843, 856, 867 and 888;
- dropping settle() at 534, 567 and 705.

Each of them goes on reading, or keeps reporting, after the budget is passed, or makes stretches up to 1,834 units where the build reports at most 267. That breaks §4.9's "stops at the report that passes it, reporting nothing more" and "256 units and one step of work at most". The existing (f) cases only reach the cap through the paths the 17 tooComplex designs happen to take.

The other survivors are equivalent:
- capacity hints;
- ties on measure-zero sets, and exact budget equality (501, 528);
- unused return values;
- init values that get overwritten;
- power-of-two axis scaling;
- sign identities of the ball-triangle orientation test (224, 227);
- comparator `<` -> `<=` on keys already unequal;
- the measure's sub-grid thresholds (Sampling 600-696);
- cadence-only settles at 262, 523, 533, 566, 590/591, 623/624, 649/650, 704, 711/712, 722/723, 885/886.
